/* =======================================================================
APP NAME: PATHOGEN BOLO & ENVIRONMENTAL SWAB INTELLIGENCE HUB (v3.0)
FILE NAME: P1.1 - pathogen bolo.txt (pathogen bolo.txt)
TARGET APP: Sanitation Inventory -> Pathogen BOLO (84a67f67-73fb-4e45-85db-0cded841bbd3)
DO NOT OVERWRITE WITH MSS CALENDAR (P0.1 - mss calendar.txt)
=======================================================================
v2.5.2 (2026-10-23) - only Gerald builds tables (data contract 1.0.62, ground rule 10 as Gerald corrected it):
- The Dataverse monitor never writes Dataverse either: it reads what each app needs from Hub config, shows it with
  prompts and steps, and tests the result. Gerald makes the tables and columns.
- Shared block hub-shared.js v1.3: the manifest also carries the recommended Copilot prompt for the _b_ Swab result
  table (written from the column types, with the exact schema names, under 2,000 characters). The monitor shows it
  with a copy button if the table is ever missing.
- The guide and the Developer view say tables are made by hand from the Dataverse monitor's list and prompts.
v2.5.1 (2026-10-23) - apps never build tables (Gerald; data contract 1.0.60, ground rule 10):
- The Developer view's table builder is gone: the recommended tables list, the ChatGPT / Copilot table prompts, the
  table probe and the schema download. Tables and columns are made by hand from the Dataverse monitor's list.
- The manifest (Hub config row manifest|bolo) gives every column BOLO needs with its type (HUB SHARED v1.2 cols, plus
  label, owner and primary for the _b_ Swab result table), so the monitor can list them and check their types.
- A table or column that is not made yet still shows on the page, with "the Dataverse monitor lists it". BOLO keeps
  reading and writing rows only: Table check and the step by step re-upload are rows, not tables.
- Ground rule 11 (headcount only in the Sanitation director) needs no change: BOLO plans no crews.
v2.5 (2026-10-23) - four views and the color rules (plan: https://claude.ai/artifact/NW9PAXQmvz1t5LLS8AtDHo):
- Four views across the top. This week: the open positives (overdue first), then last week and this week; the date
  of a day opens every swab of that day, and Pin on map puts them on the map. Trends: four headline numbers, the
  current alerts, the rate by month with last year and the target, start-up against in-process, rooms ranked. Sites:
  one page per site (every result with its state, its last cleans, the map). Data: Table check, Import check,
  targets and alert rules, Break down, What if, YoY table; for admins Upload lab files, Duplicates and Developer.
- "?" in the header opens the guide of the view; its full guide covers all four views and the admin tools. The v2.4
  picture manual and help bot are gone: they showed screens and examples that were not in the app.
- Colors follow data contract section 10 and always come with a word: red = act now (an open pathogen positive, an
  overdue one, a save that failed), amber = watch (above target, higher than last year, needs a look, an open APC /
  ATP fail), green = done, gray = not known yet (at the lab, no swabs behind a number), blue = where you are. Page,
  card and border colors are the contract's HUB_COLORS. Room colors are identity only (no red, amber, orange or green
  room); saved map areas move to the new room colors.
- Badges only for something to act on: Repeat, Email only, New since your last visit (this computer).
- A positive open more than closeDays days (PATHOGEN_BOLO_RULES, default 7) is Overdue.
- Charts: one chart per card with a legend and a Table button; last year gray, the target a dashed amber line. Creme
  vs Bakery and pathogen vs APC / ATP moved to Data, Break down.
- Map: a day's swabs as pins (a guessed spot is dashed), most urgent first, only repeat sites pulse. Reset areas is
  admin only and asks first; Remove area and Clear all ask first. A pushed pin is BOLO's own Facility Observation row
  (contract 1.0.52 / 1.0.53); a pin pushed by v2.4 had another row id, so that row is found and updated in place.
- Harborage: a concern with no photo has no picture (no drawn stand-in); removing a concern asks first.
- Removed: the old Dashboard, Graph studio and celebration pictures, and the dashboard switches in user setup.
v2.4 (2026-10-23) - the swab table is the record, and Gerald's answers:
- Every open loads the "_b_ Swab result" table and joins it to what this computer holds, so a computer whose saved
  copy is gone (Power Apps may clear it) shows every row without a re-upload. The read asks only for the columns the
  table has and skips rows marked replaced.
- Table check (top of 4. Data Manipulation Lab): swab table rows against this computer's rows, by year, with Save now
  and Read the table again. Re-upload runs one click at a time: 1. clear this computer (the table is not touched),
  2. upload every lab file (rows already in the table are not sent again), 3. the table rows no file brought back are
  listed: Mark replaced (never deleted) or Keep them. v2.3.2 marked every table row replaced before the upload while
  the upload was saving, so rows could end up marked replaced and a second re-upload was needed.
- Saves go 100 rows to a $batch request, three at a time, and wait when Dataverse says it is busy (429 / 503,
  Retry-After) instead of losing rows; a column the table lacks is left out; one PATCH a row where $batch is refused.
- APC, ATP, coliform and yeast/mold: ">250", "TNTC" and the like are past the limit, so they are fails. "est" is only
  the lab's wording: "2,500 EST" is the number 2,500. A plain APC / ATP number is a swab that did not fail, so their
  rates are fails out of every finished swab. On Listeria / Salmonella a number stays out of the rate.
- Targets and alert rules (Data tab, saved in Hub config PATHOGEN_BOLO_RULES): 2.0% pathogen, 5% APC and ATP; two
  hits at one site within 21 days is a repeat; alerts, the stage split and the surface chart look back 2 months and
  each alert shows its "since" date. The graph target line and the headline cards use the saved targets.
- Open positives: any MSS log clean of the same equipment (or area) on or after the swab day closes one (every clean
  follows the presumptive process); oldest open first, days open, owner by stage (start-up Sanitation, in-process
  Production). Positives older than the alert window are history.
- A day with results still at the lab is no longer shown as clean; the week says how many are still out.
v2.3.2 (2026-10-22) - data contract 1.0.32:
- No browser pop-ups (Power Apps blocks them, so Start over, Reset typed YoY and the bulk clear did nothing there).
  Each one now asks on the page: the button turns into "Yes, ..." and "Cancel".
- Settings (area aliases, suggested actions, harborage concerns, profiles, YoY cells, synopses, graph snapshot,
  access log) are saved to the new "_e_ Hub config" table (craa5___1_e_hubconfig) when it exists, else to the old
  craa5___1_e_hubconfig with the JSON in craa5_manifestjson, because the old craa5_configjson holds only 100 characters
  (so most saves failed). Reads take the new table first. Rows keep a fixed id per key (hubIdFromKey('hubconfig|' +
  key)), and an empty row means no settings yet.
- The app saves its table and column list once when it opens (Hub config row manifest|bolo), so the Dataverse monitor
  can check what this build needs. Shared block hub-shared.js v1.3 (since v2.5.2).
v2.3.1 (2026-10-22) - page styling:
- The page loads its own styling, like the other hub pages (https://cdn.tailwindcss.com, script id tailwind-cdn).
  Earlier versions relied on the host page and showed up unstyled where it had none. Dark mode follows the app's
  own switch. The page stays hidden up to 4 s while the styling loads; after 8 s without it, a note says so.
- The year-to-date line adds "Other programs" (no start-up / in-process timing) and "Other areas" (neither Creme nor
  Bakery), and each week adds "Other programs", so each split adds up to the total.
v2.3 (2026-10-22) - import check and honest numbers:
- One row per Sample ID + Sample Description + test (Listeria and Salmonella from one sponge are two rows). Dates are
  read as m/d/yyyy, ISO or Excel serial and never moved; result words are read again ("Not Detected" is negative, a
  number is a count with no pass/fail); columns are found by header name. Rates use finished routine (Listeria,
  Salmonella) and indicator (APC, ATP) swabs only; retests, vectors, product, water, counts and results set by hand
  are listed apart and move no rate.
- A ledger saved by v2.0-v2.2 is cleaned once on load (example rows removed, rows read again, two-test rows marked for
  re-upload). Data Manipulation opens with the Import check: a re-upload verdict, each QA email against the lab rows
  of its week, rows to look at, and Start over (clear the saved rows, optionally mark the stored Dataverse rows
  replaced, upload the lab files again).
- Calendar opens on last week, then this week (Monday to Sunday). Graphs and Data Manipulation show only numbers
  from loaded swabs: a month with no swabs is a gap, typed YoY cells only fill months with no swabs, a YoY table
  saved from v2.0 no longer brings its example numbers back, and the what-if works on real counts.
- Dataverse: rows saved under the v2.2 key are marked replaced (statecode 1 when allowed) once their v2.3 row is
  saved; craa5_result can be positive / negative / pending / count / replaced. Readers filter statecode eq 0 and skip
  replaced. Nothing is deleted.
v2.2 (2026-10-21) - shared with the ecosystem:
- Lab swab rows are saved to Dataverse table "_b_ Swab result" (craa5___1_b_swabresult), one row per Sample ID + description,
  linked by plain text keys: MSS area (craa5_area), equipment (craa5_equipmentguid), SAP work area (craa5_sapw), asset tag.
- Links come from the Swab Catalog tab (site code -> area/equipment) and zone -> MSS area settings. A blank link never
  wipes a stored one. Only admins or profiles with canIngestData write.
- A positive is closed by an MSS log row with Pathogen = Yes on the same equipment (or area) on/after the swab day.
  Open hits show on the Dashboard tab with each piece's recent MSS cleans. Status chip in the header.
v2.1 (2026-10-21) - real data only:
- Every %, count and last-year comparison is computed from loaded swab rows (or the totals in a pasted weekly email).
  A number with no swabs behind it shows "--". Plant pressure points are generic rules over real hits.
- Removed: 18k demo generator (and its rows from saved ledgers), sample email/CSV text, seeded harborage cases,
  seeded access log, fixed daily summary, built-in user list and hardcoded IDs.
- Admin tools need a real Dataverse System Administrator / System Customizer role (or the dev_admin profile in
  PATHOGEN_BOLO_USER_PROFILES_JSON); typing a name no longer unlocks them.

Purpose:
- Environmental monitoring (EMP) and pathogen BOLO hub for the Midwest Plant plant: every lab swab row (Listeria,
  Salmonella, APC, ATP and the rest) in the shared "_b_ Swab result" table, the weekly QA emails, the open positives
  and their cleans from the MSS log, the sites on the facility map and the harborage concerns.
- Numbers come only from loaded swab rows (or the totals of a pasted QA email); a number with no swabs shows "--".
- Lab files and pasted rows match on Sample ID + Sample Description + test, so a row loaded twice counts once and a
  blank (pending) result is filled in place when it comes back.
- The facility map reuses the Midwest Plant map engine (craa5___1_g_mapses, Smart Snap, blueprint fallback) without changing
  the Map submission tool; BOLO writes only its own map pin rows in Facility Observation.
- Full Light / Dark Mode with the contract's section 10 colors: blue #0072CE / #00468B for navigation and selection,
  red #DC2626 act now, amber #D97706 watch, green #059669 done, gray #64748B not known yet, each with a word.
  Brand red #E4002B is the logo only, never a status.
- HOST RULE: Avoids spreading or for-of on Set/Map; strictly 7-bit ASCII (0x00-0x7F).
======================================================================= */
